A||||10||iplayazi||What do all of you fiero owners think?||||1||
Z||000000||iplayazi||04-14-2000||12:12 PM||||Do you all think I should keep my rims or upgrade to 17" wheels?? any help is appreciated <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero.gif"> <BR>Or rims like this<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierogt.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||04-14-2000||12:40 PM||||Well, the 17's look nicer, but the rims you've got don't look bad either.  And I doubt you'd get enough of a handling benefit to justify the extra cost.  Also, those 17's will ride rough as rocks over potholes, speed bumps, tar patches, etc, and might be even be damaged by a big pothole.<P>If you lived in AZ or SoCal I'd say go for the 17's.  But being a snow belter myself I'd say keep your current rims.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||04-14-2000||12:46 PM||||Your current rims look great!  If you do decide to get the 17" wheels, LMK, your current wheels would look great on my SE!!  ||||reg||10
Z||000003||1FST2M6||04-14-2000||02:39 PM||||17s look nice handle GREAT! but can kill your 60' and 0-60 times...  the rotating mass KILLED my car and the lack of side wall flex would wipe out my 0-60 times... all it'd do was spin (245-40s on the drive tires) <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>  17s on my car.. I've since sold them.. I have 18"s that are for show only and still 2 tires short (245-35-18s are PRICEY, OUCH)... currently running stocky 14s and and STICKY tires.. I'd stick with the wheels you have and get an R compound tire and laugh at all the kids with big wheels all the way past the next light and around the corner... Show off your tail lights not just the wheels... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||04-14-2000||03:43 PM||||Is that a gold chain around your neck?  I'm just curious.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||iplayazi||04-14-2000||04:12 PM||||No its actually silver.. funny story though.. I service furnaces and I found a Silver bar that weighs about 7 pounds!  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/1nicez/images/emoticons/smokin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/1nicez/images/emoticons/smokin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/1nicez/images/emoticons/smokin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/1nicez/images/emoticons/smokin.gif"> ||||reg||1
