Z||000007||Patrick's Dad||04-14-2000||05:42 PM||||Just my 2 cents....<P>I was at the Tire Rack site, where they have a (semi)interactive rim chooser (It won't change the red 84 into a white Formula....). The 17's distract from the body line, IMO. The 16's looked better. I'd only do 17" if I could jam some 12" discs under them. I'll probably compromise with the 11¼" discs and the 16"-ers.<P>That's what makes this so fun, though. You rebuild the car the way YOU like it, and I do it the way I like it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||04-15-2000||12:27 AM||||You asked.  Here's my vote.  I love the looks of the 17" wheels, but the ones you have on look very good, too.  Save the money for other things and keep the current wheels.  However, if you did decide on the 17" wheels, I agree with turbo86se that they would look great on my fiero and would be interested.  Out of respect, though, I would only be interested if turbo86se had first shot at them and turned them down.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||04-15-2000||08:36 AM||||I think a nice balance is 16" rims. Actually, I think those are 18" on the back of the supercharged black GT. That is one sick sick car! Conversion by Chris West.||||reg||1
Z||000010||deceler8||04-15-2000||10:57 AM||||I think the 17" rims look disproportionately large on a small car like the Fiero...stick with what you have...they look great and I wish I had them on my car.||||reg||1
